Genome-wide identification and characterization of microRNAs in the domestic housefly (Musca domestica L.)
Kuznesof, Heather A.; Austin, Karen E.; Blixt, Ola;
Background: The recent advent of quantitative real-time reverse-transcription polymerase chain reaction (qRT-PCR) has expanded the capability of non-model insect studies to identify small, non-coding RNAs. Here, we use this methodology to investigate the miRNAome of the domestic housefly (Musca domestica L.) and examine potential associations with identified transcription factors. Results: We identified 1,566 microRNAs

Explanation: If the majority of a set of numbers is larger than the average, then the average of the rest of the numbers is not necessarily larger than the average.

It is therefore not possible that the majority of the numbers is larger than the average.

To test this you can add an average to the data set, for example
.mat
set nums = [12,14,15,16,17,19];
put nums.size = 6;
float total = sum(nums)/float(nums.size);

and subtract the average of the remaining numbers.
